---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import ContactUs from '../components/ContactUs.astro'
import '../styles/doc.css'
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Gammon Rivals"
  description="Privacy Policy for Gammon Rivals — what we collect, how we use it, and how to delete your account."
  canonical="https://gammonrivals.com/privacy"
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="doc-meta">
    Last updated: 4 August 2026 &middot; Data controller: Yanivos Ltd &middot;
    Tel Aviv, Israel &middot; <a href="mailto:support@gammonrivals.com">support@gammonrivals.com</a>
  </p>
  <div class="doc-note">
    Gammon Rivals is in final preparation ahead of launch, and this Policy may still
    change before then. We'll update the date above whenever it does.
  </div>

  <h2>1. About this Policy</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains what personal data we collect when you use the <em>Gammon Rivals</em> application, website, and related services (the
    &ldquo;<strong>App</strong>&rdquo;), how we use and share it, and the rights you have. It should be
    read together with our <a href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    By using the App you acknowledge the practices described here. Where we rely on your
    consent, we will ask for it separately.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    We, <strong>Yanivos Ltd</strong>, are the controller responsible for your personal
    data in connection with the App. For privacy questions or to exercise your rights,
    contact us at <a href="mailto:support@gammonrivals.com">support@gammonrivals.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. The data we collect</h2>
  <p>
    We collect what we need to run the game and to maintain and improve the App.     We <strong>do not collect payment card details</strong> &mdash; purchases are handled by the app
    stores (Section 7).
  </p>

  <h3>(a) Account &amp; identity data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>For <strong>guest play</strong>: an anonymous, device-linked account identifier generated for you. We do not require your name or email to play as a guest.</li>
    <li>If you <strong>sign in with Google</strong>: your Google account email, display name, and basic Google profile information (and a Google account identifier), as provided by Google Sign-In.</li>
    <li>A <strong>display name</strong> and profile/avatar selection shown to other players.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>(b) Gameplay &amp; game-economy data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Game progress and statistics: level, experience (XP), rating, and rankings.</li>
    <li>Virtual Currency balances (Coins, Gems) and a ledger of in-game transactions (entry amounts, prizes, bonuses, rewards).</li>
    <li>Match data: games played, moves, results, and per-turn timing used to operate matches, matchmaking, rankings, and anti-abuse.</li>
    <li>Missions, bonuses, wheel spins, owned Virtual Items (e.g., board themes), and similar feature activity.</li>
    <li>Online-presence status (whether you are currently online), used for live features.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>(c) Purchase data</h3>
  <p>
    Records of In-App Purchases and entitlements (what you bought and whether it was
    delivered). The payment itself is processed by the app store; <strong>we receive a
    confirmation/entitlement, not your card or bank details.</strong>
  </p>

  <h3>(d) Technical &amp; device data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Device and app information (e.g., device/OS type, app version, language) and general usage/diagnostic signals.</li>
    <li><strong>IP address</strong> and connection metadata, used for security, fraud/abuse prevention, and approximate region.</li>
    <li><strong>Crash and error diagnostics</strong> captured by our crash-reporting provider (Section 7), which may include device state, error/stack data, and limited context.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>(e) Communications &amp; support</h3>
  <p>If you contact support or send feedback, the content of your message and your contact details.</p>

  <h3>(f) Cookies / local storage / similar technologies</h3>
  <p>The App and website use local storage / device storage to keep you signed in and remember settings.</p>

  <h3>(g) Advertising &amp; analytics</h3>
  <p>
    The App does <strong>not currently</strong> display third-party advertising or share data with
    advertising partners. If we introduce advertising, or additional analytics beyond the
    crash/diagnostic reporting described in Section 3(d), in the future, we will update
    this Policy before doing so and, where required, ask for your consent.
  </p>

  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> knowingly collect special-category (sensitive) data, and we ask you not
    to provide it.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How we collect it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Directly from you</strong> &mdash; when you create or sign in to an account, choose a display name/avatar, make a purchase, play, or contact us.</li>
    <li><strong>Automatically</strong> &mdash; as you use the App (gameplay, device/technical, diagnostics).</li>
    <li><strong>From third parties</strong> &mdash; from Google when you choose Google Sign-In, and from the app stores when you make a purchase.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. How we use your data, and our legal bases</h2>
  <p>We use personal data to:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Examples</th><th>Legal basis (GDPR/UK GDPR)</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Provide the game &amp; your account</td><td>sign-in, save progress, balances, matchmaking, run matches</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Process &amp; honour purchases</td><td>deliver Virtual Currency/Items, reconcile entitlements, handle refunds/chargebacks</td><td>Performance of a contract; legal obligation</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Keep the App safe &amp; fair</td><td>fraud/cheat/abuse prevention, security, enforcement of the Terms</td><td>Legitimate interests; legal obligation</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Maintain &amp; improve the App</td><td>crash diagnostics, fixing bugs, reliability</td><td>Legitimate interests</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Support &amp; communications</td><td>respond to requests, send service messages</td><td>Performance of a contract; legitimate interests</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Comply with law</td><td>record-keeping, responding to lawful requests</td><td>Legal obligation</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>6. Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    We do not currently show advertising in the App, and we do not sell your personal
    data. If that changes, this section will be updated first, together with the choices
    and opt-outs that apply at that time.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Who we share it with (service providers &amp; sub-processors)</h2>
  <p>
    We share personal data with providers that process it on our behalf under contract,
    with the app stores, and where legally required. Current providers:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> &mdash; authentication, database, realtime, and file storage (our core back-end).</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> &mdash; Google Sign-In (authentication) when you choose it.</li>
    <li><strong>Apple App Store / Google Play</strong> &mdash; purchase processing for In-App Purchases, under their own terms and privacy policies.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If we add advertising or additional analytics partners, we will update this list
    before their data collection begins.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may also disclose data to comply with law or legal process, to enforce our Terms,
    to protect rights, safety, and security, or in connection with a merger, acquisition,
    or sale of assets (subject to this Policy).
  </p>

  <h2>8. International data transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Our providers may process data in countries other than yours, including the United
    States. Where we transfer personal data from the EEA/UK/Switzerland, we rely on
    appropriate safeguards such as the European Commission's Standard Contractual
    Clauses (and the UK Addendum), or another lawful transfer mechanism.
  </p>

  <h2>9. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep personal data for as long as needed to provide the App and for the purposes
    described here, then delete or anonymise it. In general:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account &amp; gameplay data</strong> &mdash; while your account is active, and for a reasonable period afterward if your account becomes inactive rather than deleted outright.</li>
    <li><strong>Purchase/transaction records</strong> &mdash; for as long as required by applicable tax, accounting, and legal obligations.</li>
    <li><strong>Crash/diagnostic data</strong> &mdash; for a limited period sufficient to investigate and fix issues.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can request deletion of your account and its data at any time (Section 10),
    rather than waiting out any retention period above.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Your rights and account deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to: access your data; correct it;
    delete it; restrict or object to processing; data portability; and withdraw consent
    (without affecting prior processing). California residents also have rights to know,
    correct, and delete, and not to be discriminated against for exercising rights.
  </p>
  <p>
    To exercise any right, contact <a href="mailto:support@gammonrivals.com">support@gammonrivals.com</a>.
    We will respond within the time required by applicable law and may need to verify
    your identity.
  </p>
  <!-- Deletion is email-only; do not restore the retired in-app flow. -->
  <p>
    <strong>Deleting your account.</strong> You can permanently delete your account and
    associated data at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:support@gammonrivals.com">support@gammonrivals.com</a> from
    the email address associated with your account. See <a href="https://gammonrivals.com/delete-account">gammonrivals.com/delete-account</a> for
    what to include in your request.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will respond within the time required by applicable law and may need to verify that
    you own the account before we act on the request. Deletion is permanent and irreversible
    and removes your account, profile, balances, transaction history, match history, and
    in-game items (it does not refund prior purchases; store-side purchase records are
    managed by Apple/Google).
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are in the EEA/UK, you may also lodge a complaint with your local data
    protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Children</h2>
  <p>
    The App is intended for users <strong>18 and over</strong> (see the Terms) and is <strong>not directed
    to children</strong>. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children. If you believe
    a child has provided us data, contact us and we will take appropriate steps to delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use technical and organisational measures designed to protect personal data,
    including access controls and database row-level security on our back-end. No system
    is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security. You are responsible
    for keeping your sign-in credentials and device secure.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Third-party services &amp; links</h2>
  <p>
    Sign-in providers, the app stores, and any third-party services you reach through the
    App are governed by their own privacy policies. We are not responsible for their
    practices.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Changes to this Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Policy from time to time. If we make material changes, we will
    provide reasonable notice (e.g., in the App or on our website) and update the
    &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date. Your continued use of the App after the changes take effect
    constitutes acceptance, except where consent is required.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Contact us</h2>
  <ContactUs />
</LegalLayout>
